.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Test photos fed to the API. Both cases are listed because case-insensitive
# matching depends on core.ignorecase, which is true on Windows but not on a
# Linux clone. heic/webp are here because phone cameras default to them.
image-test/
*.jpg
*.JPG
*.jpeg
*.JPEG
*.png
*.PNG
*.webp
*.WEBP
*.heic
*.HEIC
*.bmp
*.BMP
*.gif
*.tif
*.tiff

# Captured output from manual runs. response_example.json stays tracked —
# it is the reference payload the code is written against, not run output.
hasil.json
get_analyze_response.json
hasil*.json
.pytest_cache/

# This repository is the production deploy artifact: main.py, the recommendation
# package and the pinned dependencies. The development side of the project is
# kept on the developer's machine and deliberately not tracked here, so a clone
# is exactly what gets deployed and nothing more.
#
# What that means in practice: the tests live only locally, so a change to
# recommendation/rules.py has no safety net in this repository. The reviewed
# catalog (skincode_treatment_tags.xlsx) and the reasoning behind every clinical
# parameter are local too. Keep a backup of that directory.
CLAUDE.md
test_main.py
recommendation/README.md
recommendation_prototype/
ayuko_response_example.json
